---
id: checkbox-field
---

The pattern most forms want: a checkbox with its label and helper text. A
composition of Field and Checkbox and nothing else — the layout and spacing
come from the Field identity, the box from the Checkbox identity.

## Visual Contract

<Page>
  <Component name="CheckboxField" status="stable">
    <Instance name="field" component="Field" props={{ label: '{label}', description: '{description}', errorMessage: '{errorMessage}', error: '{error}' }}>
      <Slot name="control">
        <Instance name="box" component="Checkbox" />
      </Slot>
    </Instance>
  </Component>
</Page>

## Contract

<Props>
  <Prop name="label" type="string">The option's name.</Prop>
  <Prop name="description" type="string">Helper text under the label.</Prop>
  <Prop name="errorMessage" type="string">Validation text, shown while in error.</Prop>
  <Prop name="error" type="boolean" default={false}>Whether the field is in its error state.</Prop>
</Props>
<Composes with="Field, Checkbox" />

## Behavior

- delegation: everything the label does, Field does; everything the box does, Checkbox does. This component adds layout only.
